SUMMARY:Brumley Nature Preserve Exploration Hike PART 2
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Hiking and Outdoors Group\nWe will mostly hike trails
  we did not hike last week. We will park at the same place (see below) and
  hike the Lava Loop\, Black Cohosh\, Running Cedar\, Flat Tail (to the pon
 d we saw)\, Conservation Corps\, and the Manor Connector Trails and a smal
 l part of the Springhouse Loop. I estimate the length is 6 - 7 miles and w
 e will walk at 2.75-3 miles per hour. The autumn colors should be at their
  peak.\n\nThe Brumley Nature Preserve has several entrances so please take
  note that we are meeting at 3501 University Station Road\, Google Maps ca
 ll this "Brumley Nature Preserve Expansion".\n\nYou can find a map at the 
 website [https://triangleland.org/preserve/george-and-julia-brumley-family
 -nature-preserve](https://triangleland.org/preserve/george-and-julia-bruml
 ey-family-nature-preserve)\n\n**NOTE:** This area is sometimes closed afte
 r it has rained. I will check Sunday night and Monday morning and will can
 cel the hike by 7.30 am on Monday if the are is closed.\n\nBy participatin
 g in this event\, you agree to the terms below:\n\nTRIP PARTICIPANT WAIVER
  OF LIABILITY I fully realize that this activity involves a risk of person
 al injury\, property damage\, or loss of my person or property. I hereby f
 or myself\, my heirs\, executors and administrators\, and same for persons
  with whom are in my party\, waive and release any claims or rights agains
 t Triangle Hiking & Outdoors Group (THOG)\, all of its owners and coordina
 tors for any and all injury\, damages or loss to my person or property inc
 urred during this activity. I also understand that THOG organizers are not
  required\, nor should it be assumed that they are CPR/First Aid/Wildernes
 s Survival Certified and I am responsible for my own personal safety.
